{"status":"completed","summary":"node1 now persistently audits write and attribute-change attempts against /etc/inventory.conf using key inventory-config. Successful and denied writes were verified before and after one safe node reboot.","actions_performed":["Created /etc/audit/rules.d/inventory-config.rules with mode 0600 and rule: -w /etc/inventory.conf -p wa -k inventory-config.","Enabled and started auditd; confirmed kernel auditing and the loaded rule.","Tested a successful content change and a denied unprivileged change, restoring the original file content afterward.","Restarted node1 exactly once and verified changed boot identity, service recovery, rule persistence, unchanged target data, and fresh keyed audit events."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Persistent audit rule and healthy audit subsystem","command_ids":["cmd-46b4f2678f154060","cmd-cc693f34a8e44b24","cmd-c5d0e2a64a37415e","cmd-bcb424331269454b"],"summary":"The rule exists persistently and is loaded; auditd is active/enabled, kernel auditing is enabled, and no events were lost."},{"requirement":"Successful changes are recorded with key inventory-config","command_ids":["cmd-4750c5a723e24b66","cmd-bcb424331269454b"],"summary":"The post-restart write changed the content successfully and was restored; ausearch shows /etc/inventory.conf with success=yes and key=inventory-config."},{"requirement":"Unsuccessful changes are recorded with key inventory-config","command_ids":["cmd-bb9bca451ba84882","cmd-bcb424331269454b"],"summary":"The nobody write failed with permission denied without changing content; ausearch shows success=no, EACCES, and key=inventory-config."},{"requirement":"node1 mandatory restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-5b7752caf9044acd","cmd-a259dab43a6241f2","cmd-af4e13cb385c4ec2","cmd-61a1403962cf4d4e","cmd-bcb424331269454b"],"summary":"Healthy baseline boot ID 8ac0a119-4645-4ec4-a262-37892ad89da1 was captured, the reboot was acknowledged, and node1 returned with boot ID 9d7ea2c6-2a2c-4d93-b397-2ed9cf98d73b. auditd, the loaded/persistent rule, target checksum, and both audit outcomes recovered."}]}
